## 7. Government and Public Sector Integration Features

### 7.1 Explicit Government Permission
Section 2 (Five Freedoms) explicitly grants governments full freedom to:
- Use, modify, and distribute Waefrebeorn Work for any public-sector purpose
- Deploy Waefrebeorn models in government AI systems
- Integrate Waefrebeorn software into public digital infrastructure
- Publish modifications made by government entities back to the public domain
- Use Waefrebeorn Work in government procurement, no additional licensing fees

### 7.2 Interoperable Europe Act Compliant
This license is designed to be compatible with the Interoperable Europe Act (Regulation 2024/903) which mandates:
- FOSS adoption in public sector digital services
- Interoperability assessments for IT systems
- Cross-border sharing of reusable software components
Waefrebeorn Work can be used in all these contexts without restriction.

### 7.3 Education and Research
- Non-profit educational institutions may use Waefrebeorn Work for teaching, research, and curricular purposes without any obligation
- Public research organizations may publish results derived from Waefrebeorn Work without restriction
- Academic use is explicitly covered as Populace Freedom

### 7.4 Non-Profit and NGO Use
- Non-profit organizations may use Waefrebeorn Work for any charitable, advocacy, community, or social-purpose activity
- NGOs operating below the Populace thresholds are fully covered by the Populace exemption
- No revenue threshold limitation applies to non-profit status

### 7.5 Small Business Empowerment
- Businesses with <100 FTE and <$1M revenue are fully covered by the Populace exemption
- The license enables small businesses to compete with mega-corporations by giving them access to the same powerful tools
- No "per seat" or "per user" fees — unlimited use within the Populace definition

