## 13. Provenance

This is v3.0 of the Waefrebeorn Umbrella License, rebuilt from the v2.0 full text developed in the Waefrebeorn licensing sessions (Kevin Bacon research pass, July 2026). The dispensation clause (§5.4) is the formal mechanism for disassociating from malicious users while retaining freedom for the general population. The modifiable license reserve (§11) provides a research-backed mechanism for the Licensor to respond to emergent harms without undermining the license's core freedoms.

For the complete license text and community standards:
https://github.com/waefrebeorn/waefrebeorn-umbrella-license

For questions about licensing, commercial use, or compliance:
Contact: waefrebeorn@waefrebeorn.org

This license is not OSI-approved and not FSF-approved. It is a custom source-available license designed to protect the creator and the community.

